Falsifies `inter_process_communication::timer::verification::a_canceled_or_rearmed_timer_never_fires_stale`.

The defect: cancel reports what was pending but does not disarm it. The return value is right, so
a caller testing only what `CANCEL` returns sees nothing wrong.

Expected to fail: `assert!(got != Some(1))` once `now` passes the canceled deadline.

